            r1_brief: `June 2026. Agropecuaria Los Garabatos farms its 500 owned hectares in southern Santa Fe with machinery that can work 2,000. Aurelio Bertolini’s heirs offer La Esperanza, 300 adjoining hectares: sell it at USD 12,000 a hectare (the bank lends 70% at 7%), lease it for three campaigns at a fixed USD 420, give it in aparcería with 40% of the crop to them, or nothing. Other owners offer 400 or 800 more hectares for this campaign at USD 420. A normal year is expected (3.6 t/ha at USD 300), but the outlooks already show La Niña for 2027/28. Decide La Esperanza, the additional land and the insurance for the next two campaigns.`,
